     8	
     9	## Current — usable
    10	
    11	| Analysis | Script | What it is |
    12	|---|---|---|
    13	| **CALON-F** | `code/15_CALON_FINAL.py` | Two-cohort **incident ASCVD** model in genotype-confirmed HeFH. Spec: age (+ spline) + sex + hypertension + T2DM + smoking + cumulative non-HDL-C + TG/HDL-C. Endpoint **ASCVD only** (I21/I25/I63/I70/I73/G45); I50 heart failure excluded. UK Biobank n=3,333 / 289 events, C=0.6997; All-Wales n=1,159 / 92 events, C=0.7486. Locked 13 August 2026. |
    14	| CALON-F QC | `code/15b_QC_ADDENDUM.py` | Coefficient signs, completeness, calibration slope. |
    15	
    16	CALON-F is the only analysis in this repository whose design makes temporal
    17	leakage structurally impossible: events must be **dated after** baseline, and
    18	participants with a pre-baseline event are excluded. It does not use the
    19	mislabelled `prevalent_ascvd` field (see below), and no published score is an
    20	input to it.
    21	
    22	Head-to-head against Montreal-FH-SCORE, FH-Risk-Score and SAFEHEART-RE across 13
    23	subgroups per cohort: **10 wins, 58 ties, 1 loss** of 69 estimable cells. The
    24	single loss is UK Biobank diabetics vs SAFEHEART-RE (64 events, -0.062).
    25	
    26	**Endpoint corrected 13 August 2026.** The composite `ascvd_first_date_best`
    27	includes I50 heart failure, which is not atherosclerotic disease. 62 of 351
    28	events in the broad version were heart-failure-only. Those participants are now
    29	non-cases, censored at their recorded event date. This raised discrimination
    30	(0.6940 -> 0.6996) and reintroduced one loss that the broad endpoint had masked.
    31	The correct endpoint was preferred over the higher tally.
    32	
    33	UK Biobank calibration slope is 1.214 (1.017, 1.411) — the interval no longer
