    68	## Retracted — must not be cited as findings
    69	
    70	### 1. The cross-sectional UK Biobank arm (CALON-N and CALON-W, prevalent design)
    71	
    72	**Retracted 11 August 2026** for outcome-to-predictor temporality reversal.
    73	
    74	Every prevalent-ASCVD event pre-dated the blood draw (median 6.6 years, IQR
    75	3.8–11.6, maximum 55.6). `pre_lipid_source == "post_event_excluded"` was true for
    76	100% of cases and 0% of non-cases, and `build_ukb`'s `pre_ldl.fillna(ldl_chem)`
    77	silently restored exactly those excluded post-event, on-treatment lipid values.
    78	The model did not predict the outcome; it detected the metabolic and treatment
    79	consequences of it.
    80	
    81	**Withdrawn quantities:** the 890-participant / 57-prevalent-event cohort, its 62
    82	variant clusters, **AUC 0.7605**, **0.767**, **0.848**, **0.7672**, and the 15
    83	UK Biobank head-to-head comparisons (5 wins, 9 ties, 1 loss). These must not
    84	appear as results in any manuscript, abstract, figure, table or supplement.
    85	
    86	The material remains legitimate as an explicitly labelled **methodological
    87	negative** — a cross-sectional FH prediction analysis in which 100% of events
    88	preceded biomarker measurement, and what that does to apparent discrimination.
    89	
    90	Full record: `manuscript/TRIPOD_STROBE_PROBAST_CALON_W.md`, Section 1.
    91	
    92	Independently, the same audit found **AUC 0.7605 to be seed-favourable**: across
    93	ten cross-validation seeds the QC obtained 0.7497–0.7596, so the reported point
    94	estimate sat above the entire distribution.
    95	
    96	### 2. The FH-Risk-Score-updating architecture
    97	
    98	**Withdrawn 13 August 2026.** Feeding a published score's linear predictor into a
    99	new model, with ascertainment-specific baseline hazards, is disallowed by the
   100	programme's binding rule and its premise was falsified by measurement. See
   101	`FINAL_REPORT.md`.
   102	
   103	### 3. Comparative decision-curve analysis
   104	
   105	**Withdrawn at QC.** The comparators are ranking scores and linear predictors,
   106	not calibrated probabilities on a common scale, so net benefit is not comparable
   107	across them.
   108	
   109	### 4. The apoB effect-modification result
   110	
   111	**Withdrawn 10 August 2026** as tautological: log(apoB/LDL) = log apoB − log LDL,
   112	so interacting the ratio with apoB places apoB on both sides.
